7] [17592186145094 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186145096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145094 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186145097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145094 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186145098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145094 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186145099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145094 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145094 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145094 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c37a885d-7e2b-5e81-bc52-ff2753974527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145095 #edb/ref 1080 "32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145095 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145095 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "afbac020-f132-5e21-a592-ba884a925e15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145096 #edb/ref 1080 "35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145096 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145096 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d95d4dde-2d2e-55f4-a211-e1e0ec70664b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145097 #edb/ref 1080 "27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145097 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145097 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "de66d9e6-7a8b-5ad9-a2ad-8e52d88220f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145098 #edb/ref 1080 "30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145098 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145098 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13c043e3-9d6b-5110-b016-6b7b2ebf3cce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145099 #edb/ref 1080 "24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145099 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186145099 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "789c7308-d1a5-5b0c-9c15-595b95d781b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147162 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13108" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147162 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $4 \\%$ of $35$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147162 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "034e763d-a3e1-52e8-90a7-9fac9ce11083" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147162 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $35$, and the percentage is $4 \\%$.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n4 \\% = 4 \\div 100 = 0.04\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 4% \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= 0.04 \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= 1.4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4 \\%$ of $35$ is $1.4$.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n4 \\% = \\dfrac{4}{100}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 4% \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{100} \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= \\frac{140}{100} \\\\\n&= 1.4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4 \\%$ of $35$ is $1.4$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147163 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13109" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147163 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $140 \\%$ of $30$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147163 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a5fc07bc-6168-5525-acfb-a36ee021773d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147163 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $30$, and the percentage is $140\\%$.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140 \\% = 140 \\div 100 = 1.4\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 140% \\cdot 30 \\\\\n&= 1.4 \\cdot 30 \\\\\n&= 42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140 \\%$ of $30$ is $42$.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140 \\% = \\dfrac{140}{100} = \\dfrac{140 \\div 20}{100\\div 20} = \\dfrac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 140% \\cdot 30 \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{5} \\cdot 30 \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot \\frac{30}{5} \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140 \\%$ of $30$ is $42$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147164 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147164 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $3.6 \\%$ of $25$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147164 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8dde0f33-28c8-569b-a1f8-9390d8dafc35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147164 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $25$, and the percentage is $3.6 \\%$.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n3.6 \\% = 3.6 \\div 100 = 0.036\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 3.6% \\cdot 25 \\\\\n&= 0.036 \\cdot 25 \\\\\n&= 0.9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3.6 \\%$ of $25$ is $0.9$.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n3.6 \\% = \\dfrac{3.6}{100} = \\dfrac{3.6 \\times 10}{100 \\times 10} = \\dfrac{36}{1,000}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 3.6% \\cdot 25 \\\\\n&= \\frac{36}{1, 000} \\cdot 25 \\\\\n&= \\frac{900}{1, 000} \\\\\n&= 0.9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3.6 \\%$ of $25$ is $0.9$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147482 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147482 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147482 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147482 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147482 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147482 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147482 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding Part of a Number 